# Secrets - never commit real Spotify credentials (or anything else that
# lands in this file). Only secrets.toml.example, which has no real
# values, is meant to be tracked.
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Your personal Spotify login tokens (access/refresh token pair) written
# by the "My Spotify" tab's OAuth flow - as sensitive as a password, never
# commit this.
.streamlit/spotify_user_tokens.json

# Virtual environment
venv/
.venv/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated at runtime, not project source
results/prediction_history.csv

# Trained model artefacts - regenerable via src/train_*.py and
# src/compare_*.py (see README "Training Models" / "Model Comparison"),
# and several of these are far too large for a normal git repo -
# results/distilbert_emotion_model/model.safetensors alone is ~268MB,
# well past GitHub's 100MB hard per-file limit. Reports/tables/charts
# (.csv/.md/.png/.txt/.json under results/) are kept - those are the
# actual evidence of the ML work and are small - only the binary model
# weights themselves are excluded, EXCEPT the 3 current production
# models (emotion_model.pkl, vectorizer.pkl, audio_emotion_model.pkl -
# see the !results/... exceptions below), which are kept despite being
# binary: without them app.py can't run at all on a fresh clone or a
# hosted deploy, and at ~1.1MB/0.05MB/12.5MB they're small enough that
# there's no real reason to force a training run just to get a working
# app. The .bak rollback copies and the models_comparison/ "zoo" of
# every alternative tried are still excluded - useful locally, not
# needed for the app to function.
results/*.pkl
results/*.pkl.bak
results/*.pkl.*.bak
results/models/*.pkl
results/models_comparison/*.pkl
results/distilbert_emotion_model/
results/distilbert_v1_backup/
results/temp_recording.wav

# v2_negation_attempt keeps only small text/json evidence (report, metadata,
# probe results) - no model weights ever got copied in there, nothing to
# ignore, but listed here for clarity alongside the other distilbert entries.
!results/emotion_model.pkl
!results/vectorizer.pkl
!results/audio_emotion_model.pkl

# Third-party datasets - not this project's to redistribute (RAVDESS and
# CREMA-D both carry their own research-use licenses; the text dataset's
# redistribution terms aren't fully verified either), and the audio set
# in particular is thousands of files. See README "Dataset Requirements"
# for where to download each one - data/music.csv and
# data/afinn_sentiment_lexicon.txt are the exceptions, kept in git since
# they're this project's own curated output / a permissively-licensed
# (Apache-2.0) lexicon small enough to just include.
data/audio/
data/raw/
data/processed/

# Claude Code's local tool-permission config and test cache - machine-
# specific, not project source.
.claude/
.pytest_cache/

# Personal/dissertation artefacts, not meant for a public repo.
Notes.docx
EmotionProjectPresentation.pptx

# OS/editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Microsoft Office lock files (created while a .docx/.pptx/.xlsx is open
# elsewhere) - transient, not project content.
~$*
